The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/envelope/envelope-08-semi-implicit-infiltration-lu-allocation.md`.

**Summary of key findings:**

- **Finding 1 (High)**: The production path always builds models with `M = I` (identity), yet `build_coupled_lu` performs a full O(n³) LU factorization on an identity matrix with only 1–3 diagonal perturbations. A trivial O(n) closed-form solve is possible — just divide each coupled RHS element by `1 + d_i`.
- **Finding 2 (Medium)**: `resolve_internal` triggers two LU factorizations per timestep (one in `prepare_inputs_inner`, one in `integrate_inner`) on the same coupling data.
- **Finding 3 (Low)**: `std::mem::take` + `clone_from` pattern causes per-timestep heap allocation of the n×n matrix (~80 KB for n=100) despite the `m_scratch` field being nominally "pre-allocated."
- **Finding 4 (Low)**: When couplings are absent, the pre-factored `m_lu` is used; when couplings exist, a new LU is built despite the underlying matrix being trivially solvable.
